<title>UK: NWE gasoline tracks sideways after hefty rise.</title>
<headline>NWE gasoline tracks sideways after hefty rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gasoline was broadly steady on Wednesday after gaining up to $3 a tonne on Tuesday. Dealers said there had been little movement.</p>
<p>Interest was muted after the expected U.K. budget rise came in on Wednesday with dealers commenting the rise was in line with forecasts.</p>
<p>Traders said eurograde barges were hovering around $187.00 fob ARA with cargoes about $4 lowers.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980 (c) Reuters Limited 1997</p>
